---
import Header from "../layouts/Header.astro";
---

<Header>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-20 pb-14">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <span
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-primary/25 bg-primary/10 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary"
      >
        <span class="h-2 w-2 animate-pulse rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
        Taking on select projects
      </span>

      <h1
        class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl"
      >
        I build web &amp; mobile products — and <em
          class="text-primary not-italic">everything it takes</em
        > to ship them.
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg text-base-content/70">
        Apps, the systems around them, and the release pipelines that keep them
        moving. I've taken products from empty repo to 50,000+ monthly active
        users, and I'm deliberate about what I take on next. Right now, that
        means building for a small number of clients — and keeping the bar high
        for my next full-time role.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3.5">
        <a href="#work-with-me" class="btn btn-primary">Start a project</a>
        <a
          href="/apps"
          class="btn border-base-300 bg-base-100 font-semibold text-base-content shadow-none hover:border-base-content/40"
          >See what I've shipped</a
        >
      </div>

      <div class="mt-9 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <div>
          <strong class="block text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">0 → 50k</strong
          >
          <span class="text-sm text-base-content/50"
            >monthly active users in under 2 years</span
          >
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong class="block text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">3×</strong>
          <span class="text-sm text-base-content/50"
            >release frequency after owning CI/CD</span
          >
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong class="block text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">8+ yrs</strong>
          <span class="text-sm text-base-content/50"
            >web, mobile, cloud &amp; production delivery</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW I WORK -->
  <section class="bg-base-300 px-6 py-14">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How I work</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 mb-8 max-w-xl text-base-content/70">
        Three things you'll notice in the first two weeks of working with me.
      </p>
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="card border border-base-300 bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
          <div class="card-body p-6">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold tracking-wider text-primary">01</span>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Small releases, real conversations</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
              I ship in small increments, early and often — and I talk directly
              with the people the software is for. Scope gets refined in the
              open, not in a backlog. That's the agile manifesto as written, not
              agile as ceremony. It's rarer than it should be, and it's how
              products actually get better every week.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card border border-base-300 bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
          <div class="card-body p-6">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold tracking-wider text-primary">02</span>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Problems don't stay in my lane</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
              Every digital business is a software business, which means most
              problems — product, marketing, operations, revenue — have a
              software-shaped piece. When something is slowing the business down,
              I treat fixing it as part of the job, using whatever leverage I
              have from wherever I sit.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card border border-base-300 bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
          <div class="card-body p-6">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold tracking-wider text-primary">03</span>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Fast ramp, any stack</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
              My depth is React, React Native, Next.js, and AWS — but I've
              delivered across data visualization, DevOps automation, backend
              systems, and rapid prototyping. A new stack is a short ramp, not a
              blocker. I learn what the problem needs and get to shipping.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SERVICES -->
  <section class="px-6 py-14">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What I can do for you</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 mb-8 max-w-xl text-base-content/70">
        Engagements I'm currently taking, from a few weeks to a few months.
      </p>
      <div class="grid gap-3.5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div
          class="flex items-start gap-3.5 rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5"
        >
          <span class="font-extrabold leading-relaxed text-primary">→</span>
          <div>
            <strong class="block">MVP &amp; new product builds</strong>
            <span class="text-sm text-base-content/70"
              >From idea to a live, usable product — web, mobile, or both — with
              the infrastructure to grow.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="flex items-start gap-3.5 rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5"
        >
          <span class="font-extrabold leading-relaxed text-primary">→</span>
          <div>
            <strong class="block">Mobile apps (React Native / Expo)</strong>
            <span class="text-sm text-base-content/70"
              >iOS + Android from one codebase, through app-store review and into
              users' hands.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="flex items-start gap-3.5 rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5"
        >
          <span class="font-extrabold leading-relaxed text-primary">→</span>
          <div>
            <strong class="block">Rescue &amp; accelerate existing products</strong>
            <span class="text-sm text-base-content/70"
              >Unstick a stalled codebase, stabilize what's fragile, and get the
              release cadence back.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="flex items-start gap-3.5 rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5"
        >
          <span class="font-extrabold leading-relaxed text-primary">→</span>
          <div>
            <strong class="block">CI/CD &amp; delivery infrastructure</strong>
            <span class="text-sm text-base-content/70"
              >Pipelines, automation, and cloud setup (AWS) so shipping becomes
              routine instead of an event.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="flex items-start gap-3.5 rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5"
        >
          <span class="font-extrabold leading-relaxed text-primary">→</span>
          <div>
            <strong class="block">Fractional technical lead</strong>
            <span class="text-sm text-base-content/70"
              >Direction, code review, and delivery discipline for a small team —
              without a full-time hire.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          class="flex items-start gap-3.5 rounded-box border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5"
        >
          <span class="font-extrabold leading-relaxed text-primary">→</span>
          <div>
            <strong class="block">Not sure it fits a box?</strong>
            <span class="text-sm text-base-content/70"
              >Bring me the problem. If there's a technical path to solving it,
              I'll find it — or tell you plainly if I'm not the right person.</span
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TRACK RECORD -->
  <section class="bg-base-300 px-6 py-14">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Track record</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 mb-8 max-w-xl text-base-content/70">
        The short version. The <a href="/apps" class="text-primary">apps page</a>
        has the products themselves.
      </p>
      <div>
        <div class="relative border-l-2 border-base-content/15 pb-7 pl-6">
          <span
            class="absolute -left-[5px] top-2.5 h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-primary"
          ></span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Tactacam</h3>
          <p class="mb-1.5 text-sm text-base-content/50">
            2022–2026 · Engineer → Lead Developer
          </p>
          <p class="max-w-2xl text-sm text-base-content/70">
            Grew a React Native + Next.js platform from zero to 50,000 monthly
            active users in under two years. Led a team of five, shipped
            monetization features, and owned CI/CD — roughly tripling release
            frequency.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="relative border-l-2 border-base-content/15 pb-7 pl-6">
          <span
            class="absolute -left-[5px] top-2.5 h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-primary"
          ></span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">SAE International</h3>
          <p class="mb-1.5 text-sm text-base-content/50">2021</p>
          <p class="max-w-2xl text-sm text-base-content/70">
            Built complex onboarding flows in Angular for a core revenue product
            and contributed shared UI components used across 10+ internal
            applications.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="relative border-l-2 border-base-content/15 pl-6">
          <span
            class="absolute -left-[5px] top-2.5 h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-primary"
          ></span>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">DDI &amp; Federated Investors</h3>
          <p class="mb-1.5 text-sm text-base-content/50">2017–2020</p>
          <p class="max-w-2xl text-sm text-base-content/70">
            Data visualization, mobile development, DevOps automation, and rapid
            prototyping — frontend and backend, with production delivery
            ownership throughout.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WORK WITH ME -->
  <section id="work-with-me" class="px-6 py-14">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Work with me</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 mb-8 max-w-xl text-base-content/70">
        Tell me what you're trying to build or fix. I read every message and
        reply within one business day — usually with a question or two,
        sometimes with a sketch of how I'd approach it.
      </p>

      <!-- TODO: replace YOUR_FORM_ID with the real Formspree form ID before this goes live -->
      <form action="https://formspree.io/f/YOUR_FORM_ID" method="POST" class="max-w-2xl">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="form-control w-full">
            <span class="mb-1.5 block text-sm font-semibold">Name</span>
            <input
              type="text"
              name="name"
              required
              autocomplete="name"
              class="input input-bordered w-full"
            />
          </label>
          <label class="form-control w-full">
            <span class="mb-1.5 block text-sm font-semibold">Email</span>
            <input
              type="email"
              name="email"
              required
              autocomplete="email"
              class="input input-bordered w-full"
            />
          </label>
        </div>

        <label class="form-control mt-4 w-full">
          <span class="mb-1.5 block text-sm font-semibold"
            >Company / project <span class="font-normal text-base-content/50"
              >(optional)</span
            ></span
          >
          <input type="text" name="company" class="input input-bordered w-full" />
        </label>

        <label class="form-control mt-4 w-full">
          <span class="mb-1.5 block text-sm font-semibold">What do you need?</span>
          <select name="project_type" required class="select select-bordered w-full">
            <option value="" disabled selected>Choose one…</option>
            <option>New product / MVP</option>
            <option>Mobile app (iOS + Android)</option>
            <option>Help with an existing product</option>
            <option>CI/CD &amp; infrastructure</option>
            <option>Fractional technical lead</option>
            <option>Full-time opportunity</option>
            <option>Something else</option>
          </select>
        </label>

        <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <label class="form-control w-full">
            <span class="mb-1.5 block text-sm font-semibold"
              >Budget range <span class="font-normal text-base-content/50"
                >(optional)</span
              ></span
            >
            <select name="budget" class="select select-bordered w-full">
              <option value="" disabled selected>Choose one…</option>
              <option>Under $5k</option>
              <option>$5k – $15k</option>
              <option>$15k – $50k</option>
              <option>$50k+</option>
              <option>Not sure yet</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="form-control w-full">
            <span class="mb-1.5 block text-sm font-semibold">Timeline</span>
            <select name="timeline" required class="select select-bordered w-full">
              <option value="" disabled selected>Choose one…</option>
              <option>ASAP</option>
              <option>Within 1–2 months</option>
              <option>This quarter</option>
              <option>Just exploring</option>
            </select>
          </label>
        </div>

        <label class="form-control mt-4 w-full">
          <span class="mb-1.5 block text-sm font-semibold"
            >The problem, in your own words</span
          >
          <textarea
            name="message"
            required
            placeholder="What are you building, what's in the way, and what does success look like?"
            class="textarea textarea-bordered min-h-32 w-full"></textarea>
        </label>

        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary mt-6">Send it my way</button>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-base-content/50">
          Prefer email? <a href="mailto:23mwest@gmail.com" class="text-primary"
            >23mwest@gmail.com</a
          > — same inbox, same response time.
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <footer class="border-t border-base-300 px-6 py-10">
    <div
      class="max-w-4xl mx-auto flex flex-wrap justify-between gap-4 text-sm text-base-content/50"
    >
      <span
        >Michael J West · Pittsburgh, PA · B.S. Computer Engineering, University
        of Pittsburgh</span
      >
      <span class="flex gap-4">
        <a class="hover:text-base-content" href="https://github.com/23mwest"
          >GitHub</a
        >
        <a
          class="hover:text-base-content"
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/michaeljosephwest">LinkedIn</a
        >
        <a class="hover:text-base-content" href="mailto:23mwest@gmail.com">Email</a>
      </span>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Header>
